{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for hosted MCP head e0aa08e5da84d4363d16b068768f1f2d9f68ec46, tree 95370d60d0f5ef747635f0a88065ac004f55ee44. Normal preparation binds all 27 artifacts to original request 9b3084d4. I completed the primary first through my own E31 full read, independently verified exact unchanged byte ranges, and read every new byte. Four parallel reports were read completely; the following findings are independently corroborated by my selected complete source units. No runtime or test execution by checker.\n\nThe prior refused-initialize P2 and UTF-8 P3 are repaired. Admission validates and durably keeps the newcomer before inserting it or ending the oldest; Wire catches arbitrary persistence-hook failure, allowing refusal cleanup. Capabilities and inspected control accounting use encoded UTF-8 bytes. Earlier control, retirement, terminal-step reservation and replacement-stream repairs remain credited.\n\n1. P2: failed tools/list persistence advances the live listed marker (packages/mcp/src/wire.ts:222–223; hosted.ts:341–350; http.ts:258–291). A session previously listed A; inventory becomes B; tools/list assigns live listed=B, but the session-row SQL write fails and rolls back. Wire returns a correlated internal error, so no B list was delivered, while durable listed remains A. A reconnect at B compares against live B and suppresses the change; the watcher does likewise. Reset restores A and changes the behavior. A-to-B digests have equal length: this counterexample uses a storage write failure, not an assertion that a full-budget relist necessarily grows its row. Persist prospective session state before committing the live marker, or restore it on failure. Witness the failed write, correlated error, reconnect without reset notifying B once, then successful B listing suppressing further reconciliation. Keep other mutable durable fields consistent too.\n\n2. P2: completion-budget admission occurs after signing (custody.ts:281–300, service.ts:393–434, sqlite-custody.ts:97–106 and193). #kept checks byte/count limits, then build signs the new intent and writes its prepared record. SQLite arms completion capacity only on the later dispatch write. If the prepared row fits but another completion need does not, full is returned after a signature and durable preparation; even an exhausted stored budget is detected after build. Adopted H6 explicitly requires new admission refusal before signing. The new saturated-budget case626–653 counts one native act, which proves no second dispatch, not zero signatures. Reserve or refuse the new identity's completion need under exclusive admission before build/signing; preserve existing envelopes and outstanding reservations. Add signing/build and prepared-record assertions to this case, then verify settlement and later admission still work.\n\n3. Required commissioned acceptance remains incomplete. H1's five faults now fire, but test589–625 never captures the original seed/key, kept signed envelope or completed bearer before the reset. Replacing an unsent envelope while retaining its key can still produce one final enrolment and stable post-retry answers, passing the test. Capture and compare the original durable values and admitted bytes at the relevant fences. Production custody preservation is credited; this is an inadequate witness, not proof it replaces an envelope. H5 modern reset373–387 never awaits old-stream EOF; Worker585 merely clears the cached agent, and the old response retains its HTTP/Wire through closures. A silently open old body passes until both streams are manually aborted. Provide actual abrupt teardown and assert EOF without a final event before reconnect. The full-budget incumbent check573–578 is conditional after catch-to-null and can pass without an incumbent. H6 still owes the adopted prepared-reset, concurrent send/settle, 255-unresolved admission, archived-refusal/full/recovery, repeated uncertain top-up/reset, full CREATE and archived terminal replay scenarios; store-lock/direct-write tests do not replace these custody/endpoint duties. H7's size-only helper432–442 accepts small errors and does not exercise the commissioned large/paginated plan031 budget witnesses. Preserve the original matrix and assert successful intended outcomes.\n\nArchitecture: shared transport and separate durable listed/per-stream notified state remain sound choices; commit ordering must keep durable and live truth aligned. Security: budget refusal must precede signing, while existing authority, bearer and origin boundaries stay intact. Simplification: atomic prospective state and explicit admission make these invariants easier to test than recovery from partially committed state.\n\nEvidence limits: only the scope-named closed gate index and public-result JSON were admitted, hash/size checked before complete reads. Their native head/tree match. The owner projection reports one original gate, exit0, whitespace/typecheck/tests0, 1168 passes and3 unrun skips, installation skipped. Scripted resets and the pre-existing retention-fault log message are owner observations; raw logs and their causes were not verified. No other indexed file was read. Native census finds 27 owned changed paths and all1493 outside receiving27bb entries exact, rather than the note/projection's25. Current main2a40 also has the sealed Counter note absent from this candidate; preserve it and all later receiving work during normal composition. Whole source files outside the explicitly reviewed units remain honestly partial; peer whole-body coverage is not borrowed.\n\nOriginal9b explicitly requires source review/landing, then pinned scratch deployment and a live check in a note-only delivery. Those post-landing duties remain owed. OAuth, export, pinned reads, resources/prompts and Start parity remain outside this source head and are not accepted here. Critical cross-room request2ce now takes priority; this ready verdict claims no security-fix acceptance.","body"